---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ContentFlow App | Why it exists"
  description="Why ContentFlow App exists and which workflows it is built to make reliable."
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <NavBar />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">About ContentFlow App</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Built to keep content execution reliable, not brittle.</h1>
        <p>
          ContentFlow App is the authenticated operations surface for creators and
          lean teams that want to move from ideas to publish-ready planning with
          continuity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <article class="price-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Who It Is For</p>
          <h2>Creators, solo builders, and small content teams</h2>
          <p>
            The app is for people running multiple content surfaces who need one
            coherent place to coordinate ideas, status, schedules, and review
            state.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="price-card accent-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Primary Problem</p>
          <h2>Broken continuity</h2>
          <p>
            The main friction is not feature count. It is losing momentum when APIs
            are unstable, work is fragmented, or action states are unclear.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What It Is Not</p>
        <h2>No replacement for editorial judgment.</h2>
        <p>
          ContentFlow App is explicitly human-led. It supports operators with
          reliable state, queue visibility, and actionable diagnostics while people
          keep the final decision.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Positioning from repo</h3>
          <p>
            The product context defines ContentFlow as an execution layer in a larger
            ecosystem, not a standalone AI factory.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Core constraints</h3>
          <p>
            In-app reliability is prioritized over feature shortcuts. Offline reads,
            queue replay, and clear state transitions are part of the baseline
            behavior.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="cta-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Next Step</p>
        <h2>Read the operational docs, then inspect the workflow map.</h2>
        <p>
          Start with core docs and the capabilities page for a practical sense of
          what is shipped and what is explicitly out of scope.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs">Open documentation</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/skills">Browse workflows</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/faq">Read FAQ</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
